---
description: SyncSpace Deutsch product and architecture rules
alwaysApply: true
---

SyncSpace Deutsch is a deterministic collaborative German study tool, not an AI wrapper.

Read `docs/project-context.md`, `docs/versions.md`, `docs/conflict-policy.md`, `docs/architecture-decisions/adr-s08-hosted-trusted-group.md`, and `AGENTS.md` before changing shared/private ownership, schema, deletion, grading, room access, or hosted sync bind/CORS.

Use separate status language: saved on this device, connected, initial synchronization complete, server checkpoint recorded.

Seed shared rooms once on the server. Persist binary Yjs state. Keep review events out of Yjs, awareness, exports, and the sync server.

Starter German stays draft until a human review is recorded. Do not fabricate that review.

Never commit room tokens. Do not commit or push unless the user asks.
